            "notes": "Checks how far the system clock is off from the time chronyd derives from its NTP servers, in milliseconds, and how long ago chronyd last synchronized it. Alerts when the offset or the time since the last synchronization exceeds the configured thresholds, when the stratum is too high, when too few NTP sources are usable, or when chronyd uses no NTP server, including when it only serves its local clock.",
